.nh
.TH "GMB" "1" "Sep 2026" "GlassMarble 1.1.0" "GlassMarble Manual"

.SH NAME
gmb-doc-init - Scaffold a new managed document with AKG-grounded sections


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgmb doc init  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Scaffolds a new living document and adds its specification to
\&.glassmarble/docs.yaml.

.PP
Runs an interactive questionnaire (Title, Purpose, Audience, Archetype,
Scope, Entry Points) unless --scope is given, which switches to
non-interactive mode and requires every other field as a flag.

.PP
Entry points seed call-graph/sequence diagrams and are NOT auto-detected:
an archetype whose sections include a callgraph or sequence diagram (most
of them do) renders that diagram as an empty placeholder until at least
one entry point is set, here or later by hand-editing docs.yaml's
entry_points key for the document.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--archetype\fP=""
	Built-in document template: architecture|module|runbook|onboarding|migration|adr|api|security|database|config

.PP
\fB--audience\fP=""
	Intended reader (e.g. 'On-call SRE engineers')

.PP
\fB--entry-points\fP=[]
	FQNs seeding call-graph/sequence diagrams (e.g. 'internal/auth/service.go::Authenticate'); without at least one, this archetype's diagrams stay empty; repeat the flag or comma-separate for multiple

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for init

.PP
\fB--id\fP=""
	Stable document ID (default: derived from target path)

.PP
\fB--purpose\fP=""
	One-sentence description of what the document is for

.PP
\fB--scope\fP=[]
	Glob patterns for this document's scope (e.g. 'internal/auth/**'); repeat the flag or comma-separate for multiple

.PP
\fB--title\fP=""
	Document title


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--color\fP="auto"
	Color output mode: auto|always|never

.PP
\fB-c\fP, \fB--config\fP=""
	Config file path (default is $HOME/.glassmarble.yaml)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug logging

.PP
\fB--dir\fP=""
	Target repository directory for analysis and queries

.PP
\fB--max-json-mb\fP=0
	Refuse to load or commit an AKG state file (akg.json) larger than this many MiB (0 = unlimited)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Suppress non-error output

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	Verbose output logging


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # Scaffold a new module reference
  gmb doc init docs/auth.md

  # Scaffold with a specific archetype
  gmb doc init docs/runbook.md --archetype runbook

  # Scaffold with a pre-set scope (non-interactive)
  gmb doc init docs/storage.md --scope "internal/storage/**" --archetype module

  # Non-interactive with an entry point so call-graph diagrams populate
  gmb doc init docs/auth.md --scope "internal/auth/**" --archetype module \\
    --entry-points "internal/auth/service.go::Authenticate"
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgmb-doc(1)\fP


